{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-143842-r4518549","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Cincinnati-Style Chili","sourcePageId":143842,"sourceRevision":"4518549","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:29:23Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Cincinnati-Style%20Chili&oldid=4518549","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:16.285Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for chili","Category:Recipes using allspice","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using chili powder","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using ground beef","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using marjoram","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Refrigerated recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d6e801b9fa361d85925deca0ebceb6d75ad3e9f36726327538e1570dfd7f7b12","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Stew recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] ground [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Quart|quart]] cold water\n* 1 can (6 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* 2 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 cloves of [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n* 1 tablespoon salt\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]]\n* ¼ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Marjoram|marjoram]]\n* ⅛ teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Crumble the raw ground beef into the cold water.\n#Add remaining ingredients and spices. Stir well, breaking the meat up before cooking.\n#Cover and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] over low heat for two hours, stirring occasionally.\n#Cool, then refrigerate and remove solidified grease.\n#Reheat and serve as desired.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Serve over spaghetti. Top with cheese to make a Three-way, top with onions and cheese to make a Four-way, top with cooked pinto beans, onions and cheese to make a Five-way. May also be used as hot dog sauce with mustard and minced onions to make a Coney, adding shredded cheese to make a Cheese Coney.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for chili]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef]]\n[[Category:Midwestern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Refrigerated recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using allspice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marjoram]]","isRecipe":true,